\caption(Two valid arithmetic exchanges give the intermediary two different shared residues. The legacy wrappers also accept zero, identity and order-two peer values; successful powering is not protocol validation.)
\alttext(Three native boxes show Alice with raw shared 18, an intermediary knowing 18 and 15, and Bob with raw shared 15. The footer gives the substituted public values 21 and 17.)

A received zero can force zero for positive exponents; one always gives one;
p−1 reveals exponent parity in these examples. Range and subgroup validation
belong to a fully specified group/protocol. For known safe-prime FFDHE groups,
[RFC 7919 section 5.1](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7919.html#section-5.1)
specifies 1<Y<p−1; its discussion of unknown groups requires more than that
range check. Our toy full-group generator and arithmetic APIs do not claim to
implement that RFC. Authenticating the exchange and deriving a usable key
are separate tasks absent from this demonstration.

> Count actual work and check the full-width arithmetic

For m>1 and positive exponent e, let L=bit_width(e) and w=popcount(e). The
retained right-to-left loop performs exactly L squares and w accumulator
products, including its final unused square:

$$
N_{\mathrm{products}}=L+w.
$$
\alttext(The number of modular products equals the exponent bit width plus its number of one bits.)

At the same L, a power-of-two exponent takes L+1 products while an all-one
exponent takes 2L. Thus the implementation is not constant-time; this plot
counts operations, without treating them as measured processor timings.
Exponent zero has no products and returns one for m>1; m=1 returns zero
without products for any exponent. Both scalar and trace reject m=0.
The work sweep uses modulus 2^64−1 as an arithmetic control, not a prime field.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/dh_power_work.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  std::vector<double> bits,sparse,dense;const auto maximum=std::numeric_limits<std::uint64_t>::max();
  std::print("| exponent bits | sparse one bits | sparse products | dense one bits | dense products |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
  for(unsigned k:{1,2,4,8,16,32,64}) {
    const auto e1=std::uint64_t{1}<<(k-1),e2=maximum>>(64-k);
    const auto a=dm::algorithms::mod_pow_trace(maximum-1,e1,maximum),b=dm::algorithms::mod_pow_trace(maximum-1,e2,maximum);
    if(a.work.products!=k+1 || b.work.products!=2*k)return 1;
    bits.push_back(k);sparse.push_back(a.work.products);dense.push_back(b.work.products);
    std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n",k,a.work.accumulator_products,a.work.products,b.work.accumulator_products,b.work.products);
  }
  auto p=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();p.line(bits,sparse,"one set bit",{37,99,235},2).points(bits,sparse,"one set bit",{37,99,235},5)
   .line(bits,dense,"all bits set",{234,88,12},2).points(bits,dense,"all bits set",{234,88,12},5)
   .legend({"one set bit","all bits set"},{{37,99,235},{234,88,12}})
   .title("Same exponent width, different actual modular-product counts").x_label("exponent bit width L").y_label("actual modular products, including final square")
   .y_limits(0,160).size(1100,570).save_svg("build/dh_power_work.svg");
  const auto exact=dm::algorithms::mul_mod(maximum-1,maximum-2,maximum),wrapped=((maximum-1)*(maximum-2))%maximum;
  std::print("\nFull-width product modulo UINT64_MAX: exact {}; prematurely wrapped 64-bit arithmetic {}.\n\n",exact,wrapped);if(exact!=2 || wrapped!=6)return 1;
  const auto zero=dm::algorithms::mod_pow_trace(0,0,23),unit=dm::algorithms::mod_pow_trace(maximum,maximum,1,1);
  std::print("Zero exponent: result {}; products {}. Unit modulus: result {}; products {}.\n\n",zero.result,zero.work.products,unit.result,unit.work.products);
  int rejected=0;
  try{dm::algorithms::mul_mod(1,1,0);}catch(const std::invalid_argument&){++rejected;}
  try{dm::algorithms::mod_pow_trace(5,6,23,2);}catch(const std::length_error&){++rejected;}
  try{dm::algorithms::dh_power_cycle(5,23,21);}catch(const std::length_error&){++rejected;}
  try{dm::algorithms::dh_power_cycle(1,15,1);}catch(const std::invalid_argument&){++rejected;}
  const auto exact_bits=dm::algorithms::mod_pow_trace(5,6,23,3),uncapped_bits=dm::algorithms::mod_pow_trace(5,6,23,0);
  const auto exact_cycle=dm::algorithms::dh_power_cycle(5,23,22);
  if(rejected!=4 || exact_bits.result!=uncapped_bits.result || exact_cycle.order!=22)return 1;
  std::print("Four expected modulus/cap/composite rejections: {}. Exact caps 3 bits and 22 cycle values succeed; zero disables optional caps.\n",rejected);
}
